b80['questions']['core_calibrated'][3]=Q(4,'B80','A particle goes from −3 m to +5 m, then returns to +1 m. Find distance and displacement. A second observer adds 10 m to every coordinate. What changes?',1,'Route −3 → +5 → +1 m; then shift every coordinate by +10 m.','Displacement is a coordinate difference, so a common shift cancels.','Path lengths: 5 − (−3) = 8 m and 5 − 1 = 4 m. Δx = 1 − (−3) = +4 m. Shifted endpoints are +7 m and +11 m.','Distance 12 m and displacement +4 m for both origins. Positions change.','A reference origin changes position values, not a fixed journey.', ['The second observer changes the labels, not the physical journey.','Draw the three positions, then label each with 10 m added.','Compare (1 + 10) − (−3 + 10) with 1 − (−3).'],'B80-L1',task_type='Transfer',numeric={'kind':'route','positions':[-3,5,1],'distance':12,'displacement':4})
b80['questions']['core_calibrated'][4]=Q(5,'B80','Journey A: +3 m/s for 4 s, then +2 m/s for 2 s. Journey B changes only the last velocity to −2 m/s. Find both distances and displacements. Explain what stays the same.',2,'A: +3 for 4 s, then +2 for 2 s. B: last velocity becomes −2 m/s.','Reversing the second velocity changes the area sign, not its size.','First area is +12 m in both. The last area is +4 m in A and −4 m in B. Add signs for displacement and sizes for distance.','A: Δx = +16 m, distance 16 m. B: Δx = +8 m, distance 16 m.','A sign change can alter the endpoint without altering total path.', ['Only the direction of the last interval changes.','Sketch the two graphs with the same scales.','Calculate the common first area: (+3 m/s) × (4 s).'],'B80-L2',task_type='Compare',numeric=None)
